      en: "Yankari National Park is Nigeria's most famous and spectacular wildlife reserve, located in the savanna woodlands of Bauchi State. Originally established as a game reserve in 1956 and later upgraded to a national park, it covers an immense area of over 2,200 square kilometers. Yankari is the absolute premier destination for eco-tourism in West Africa, uniquely renowned for hosting the largest surviving elephant population in the country. The park's most magical feature is the Wikki Warm Springs, a crystal-clear, naturally heated pool where visitors can swim year-round. It remains a critical stronghold for biodiversity, including lions, buffalo, and hundreds of bird species. Geography K8 — savanna wildlife reserves and eco-tourism."
